{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'I1|3\\\\.5|3\\\\.6|Scatter|scatter' docs/02-product-spec.md docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md && rg -n 'Lookup|pick\\\\(' packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts\"","aggregated_output":"docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:3:Revision 3, 2026-11-18. Revised after three independent reviews ([ledger](../reviews/2026-11-18/ledger.md)) and the owner's decisions of the same day (scatter and a compact variant are in 1.0; the mark renderer is decided in M1).\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:34:| One function per chart type (`line`, `area`, `bar`, `donut`, `scatter`) | Each has its own options type, so options that do not apply are type errors (DX3), and bundlers can drop unused chart types. Whether shared code actually tree-shakes is measured on real consumer builds in M7. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:60:| Order | Line, area and scatter are sorted by x internally (F11). `append` expects rows at or after the last x. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:103:| `strict`, `onDiagnostic` | Diagnostics delivery (section 3.5 of the spec). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:132:The registry, with each code's level and outcome, is in the spec (section 3.5). Example for the Phase 1 combined dirty fixture (`[10, 20, null, NaN, '40', undefined, 70]`):\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:185:| lookup | Nearest-x by binary search; nearest-point by a grid index (scatter) | Works on the frame within the visible range; cost bounded independently of the drawing. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:298:- Title, `labelledBy`, subtitle, axis titles; toolbar with legend toggles; full tooltip and fixed readout (I1); label fitting (L1) and the too-small fallback (L8); states (L7); reference lines and bands.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:322:### M5. Bar, area, donut, scatter and the compact variant (ceiling: 18 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:324:Each type is done when its column of the type matrix (spec 3.6) and every applicable row of the acceptance matrix pass, including the accessibility and performance rows. Types are finished one at a time, in this order: bar, area, donut, the compact variant, scatter.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:332:- Scatter: picking, ties, coincident points and a clustered-data benchmark.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:3:Revision 3, 2026-11-18. Revised after three independent reviews ([ledger](../reviews/2026-11-18/ledger.md)), then updated with the owner's decisions of the same day: scatter is in 1.0, a compact variant is in 1.0, and the mark renderer is decided by measurement in M1.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:56:| Scatter | Optional series | How are two measures related? | 1.0 (owner's decision) |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:61:The Phase 1 harness exercised line, bar and donut in all ten libraries (donut in nine; uPlot has none). Area and scatter are added on judgment; Phase 1 found no usage data by chart type. Two reviewers argued for fewer types and one for a compact variant; the owner decided on all five types plus the compact variant. Scatter alone needs two-dimensional hit testing and its own navigation model, so it is built last and carries the most schedule risk.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:63:Each type has its own rules for picking, navigation and limits. They are in the type matrix in section 3.6, and a type does not ship until its row is fully tested.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:96:| F3 | Input that cannot be plotted as given is reported, never guessed. The diagnostic registry (section 3.5) fixes each case's level, what is drawn and what the reader sees. | One test per code; the combined `dirty` fixture and the four one-bad-value fixtures yield exactly the codes listed in section 3.5 | R5, D5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:104:| F11 | Line, area and scatter are drawn in x order whatever the input order. On line, area and bar, two rows with the same x in one series are AX108 and that series is not drawn. On scatter, points sharing an x (or both coordinates) are ordinary data. | Shuffled `trend` renders identically; duplicate fixture | R5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:124:| I1 | Pointing anywhere in the plot shows what is there, by the picking rule for the chart type (section 3.6), within one frame at the 95th percentile. On line, area and bar the tooltip lists every visible series at the nearest x; a series with no row at that x reads \"No observation\", distinct from \"No data\". The tooltip stays inside the viewport, does not cover the active mark, can itself be hovered, and lists at most eight rows plus \"+N more\". When it cannot fit, the same content appears in a fixed readout under the plot. Escape closes it until the pointer reaches a different datum. | Hover at 20 positions including all four edges; sparse-series fixture; narrow tile with eight series; Escape test | R15 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:148:### 3.5 Diagnostic registry\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:178:| AX133 | Hint | A scatter chart has more than 50,000 points | Drawn; the message says drawing may be slow |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:179:| AX134 | Error | Series × x positions exceeds 20,000,000 (long rows with many series and little shared x) | Error state; the message gives both counts and suggests fewer series or a scatter chart |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:188:### 3.6 Type matrix\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:190:| | Line | Area | Bar | Donut | Scatter |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:225:| DX4 | Diagnostics follow the registry in section 3.5: stable code, chart name, field and rows where they apply, the fix, and a documentation page per code. | Message snapshots; link checker | R5, D5 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:262:| Diagnostics are a first-class feature with codes | R5: none of the ten named the field, the row or the problem. | Kept. Severity and delivery rewritten (3.5): readers are told too, and production builds are not silent. |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:292:Settled by the owner on 2026-11-18: scatter is in 1.0; the compact variant is in 1.0; the mark renderer stays open until M1 measures both.\n628:export interface Lookup {\n630:  pick(px: number, py: number): PickTarget | null;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
